                <pb facs="0822" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/484a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-01T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>114. For General Crowder:</p>
                <p>The Department has been advised by representative of certain New York banking
                    interests that bankers are disposed to make the Cuban Government a loan up to
                    $50,000,000 if Cuba desires it. If the Zayas administration desires such a loan
                    as the one mentioned cable the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
